      "side": 1,
      "message": "`isAi` here is the commit-level `Is-ai` footer parsed for the current `ChangeNotesCommit`, not a property of the copied approval. Just as `parseCopiedApproval` uses `parsedPatchSetApproval.tag()` rather than the commit-level `tag` field, it should not set `.isAi(isAi)` from the commit-level `isAi` field (otherwise, if a commit that writes `Copied-Label` footers also has `Is-ai: true`, every copied approval in that commit—including human votes from other reviewers—would be marked `isAi \u003d true`).",
